.TITLE "find"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Searches for files and directories in a directory hierarchy based on various __criteria__. It can find items by __name__, __size__, __type__, or __time__.

.DIV "TLDR"
**find path -name "pattern"**
Searches for files matching a specific name pattern within a path.
> __path__ search location | __-name__ name flag | __"pattern"__ search term

**find path -type type**
Filters the search results by file type, such as directories or regular files.
> __path__ location | __-type__ type flag | __type__ f (file) or d (directory)

**find path -size +value**
Finds files that are larger than a specific size.
> __path__ location | __-size__ size flag | __+value__ size (e.g., +100M)

**find path -mtime -days**
Searches for files modified within a specific number of days.
> __path__ location | __-mtime__ modification time flag | __-days__ day count

**find path -name "pattern" -delete**
Finds and immediately removes files that match the criteria.
> __path__ location | __-delete__ deletion flag | __"pattern"__ search term

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __find__ command is extremely versatile; you can chain multiple criteria together to perform complex searches. Always run your search without __-delete__ first to verify the results before performing a mass deletion.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:grep** **linux:locate** **linux:xargs**

